tier: opus
branch: feat/work-observability
depends_on:
owns: src/charon/engine/scheduler.py, src/charon/cli.py, src/charon/proxy_server.py, src/charon/service/   # PROVISIONAL — finalize at activation
prompt: (authored on activation)
scope: PRODUCTION-READINESS. Close the work-engine OBSERVABILITY gap. VERIFIED IN CODE
  2026-06-27: when a user runs tickets via `charon work` / `run`, there is NO live
  observability — the run is SILENT and then prints a single final JSON blob. The engine
  (`engine/scheduler.py` `drain`) has ZERO print/logging. The ACP agent's output is discarded
  (stderr → DEVNULL, tokens not relayed; see `adapters/acp.py`). The only record is per-unit
  `charon ledger <id>` plus hand-tailing `.charon/work-board.json` and
  `.charon/<id>/checkpoints.jsonl`. The gateway web console (`proxy_server.py`) shows only
  gateway traffic — no work/board state. A separate Mode-B dashboard exists
  (`python -m charon.service`) but is NOT wired to any subcommand, only polls, and is fed by
  `run_task` — NOT the `work` engine. ADR-0004 D7 explicitly DEFERRED the "watch the agent"
  live view; it was never built. This ticket builds it.

  SUB-GOALS (design phase picks which ship first — they need not all land at once):
  1. **Live progress for `charon work` / `run`.** Emit per-unit lifecycle lines
     (claimed / started / checks / land / done / blocked) and/or a live board view as the
     scheduler drains. Today the run is silent until the final JSON.
  2. **Capture the agent's work.** Optionally persist each unit's ACP transcript/output to a
     per-unit log under `.charon/<id>/` (today stderr → DEVNULL, tokens unrelayed) so a user can
     inspect what the agent actually did beyond the commit diff + terse note.
  3. **Aggregate run view.** A command (or an extension of `ledger`) that rolls up a WHOLE
     `work` run — all units' status / cost / PRs — not just the per-unit `ledger <id>`.
  4. **Surface work state in a UI.** Either add a work/board panel to the gateway console, OR
     wire the Mode-B service dashboard to the `work` engine and to a `charon` subcommand (it
     currently needs `python -m charon.service` + the service extra, only covers `run_task`, and
     only polls).

  CONSTRAINTS: must NOT bloat the gateway-first hot request path (anti-dilution) — observability
  stays in the opt-in engine/CLI path, never the per-request gateway path; product-clean (no
  SLOP/fleet/rig leak); agent/provider-agnostic; stdlib-only privileged core.
note: PARKED. PRODUCTION-READINESS — `charon work` is a black box during a run (no live
  progress, agent output uncaptured, no aggregate/work UI). ADR-0004 D7 deferred the live
  watcher; this builds it. Activate when work-engine UX is prioritized.

## NOTE — PARKED, NOT CLAIMABLE

**This is a production-readiness BUILD ticket staged `.parked`.** It captures the work-engine
observability gap verified in code 2026-06-27 (see scope). It stays `.parked` (not yet
claimable) pending activation: pick which sub-goals ship first, author the work-spec prompt, and
finalize `owns:`.

TYPE: **build** (engine + CLI, possibly UI). `depends_on` EMPTY (board-unblocked). `owns:` is
PROVISIONAL — `src/charon/engine/scheduler.py`, `src/charon/cli.py`, `src/charon/proxy_server.py`,
`src/charon/service/` is the likely surface; finalize the exact file set at activation (and
confirm disjoint within its wave vs any concurrent ticket touching `cli.py` / `proxy_server.py`
before launch, so it does not collide). If the design adds a NEW observability module rather than
growing the scheduler, add it to `owns:` then.

Un-park / activation checklist:
1. Pick which sub-goals (1–4) ship in the first PR vs follow-ons (sub-goal 4 / the UI may split
   into its own ticket if the engine+CLI PR gets large).
2. Author the work-spec prompt at `../prompts/work-observability.md` (ends with the CONSTRAINTS
   block: own ONLY the files in `owns:`).
3. Finalize `owns:` (confirm disjoint within its wave vs any concurrent `cli.py` /
   `proxy_server.py` ticket) and drop this to an active `board/WORK-OBSERVABILITY.md`.
4. `bash validate_board.sh` GREEN before launching.
